    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Jacqui Irwin is a member of the California State Assembly and a former mayor and city councilmember of Thousand Oaks. She has worked as an engineer at Teledyne Systems and the Johns Hopkins University Applied Physics Lab. Her campaign says she has passed 86 laws in the state legislature focusing on consumer rights, education, and cybersecurity. Those include securing $3 million for local law enforcement to recover firearms from people prohibited from possessing them and creating tax-free savings accounts for people with disabilities. She supports policies that hold polluters accountable to help lower electricity bills.",
        "cites": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Jacqui Irwin is a member of the California State Assembly and a former mayor and city councilmember of Thousand Oaks.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "She has worked as an engineer at Teledyne Systems and the Johns Hopkins University Applied Physics Lab.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "Her campaign says she has passed 86 laws in the state legislature focusing on consumer rights, education, and cybersecurity.",
            "cites": [3]
          },
          {
            "text": "Those include securing $3 million for local law enforcement to recover firearms from people prohibited from possessing them and creating tax-free savings accounts for people with disabilities.",
            "cites": [4]
          },
          {
            "text": "She supports policies that hold polluters accountable to help lower electricity bills.",
            "cites": [5]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "She says reducing the cost of housing, energy, and food is a top priority. She wants tax reductions given to utilities to be passed on to ratepayers instead of shareholders. She wants to restore access to affordable healthcare and opposes recent cuts. She supports reforming the immigration system and securing the border. She says states should remain responsible for conducting elections.",
        "cites": [5],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "She says reducing the cost of housing, energy, and food is a top priority.",
            "cites": [5]
